From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:38:32 -0400
Subject: feat: import from Dia and from Safari's export file

Welcome step 2 gains an "Everything from Dia" block and a "Safari's
export file" row (docs/features/import.md I28-I32, I34-I42).

- Dia: its User Data found on the Mac and in two Windows places (I28);
  bookmarks into "Imported from Dia" (I29); history from a copy that
  carries the write-ahead log (I30); passwords unsealed with the
  keychain item looked up by service, or Local State's DPAPI key, the
  key read only after the button, "v20" values counted (I31); a summary
  that reads no key (I32).
- Safari's export, as the archive or its folder (I34): read by
  Chromium's Rust archive reader, the bookmarks page and the passwords
  file parsed in utility processes, every part size-checked (I35); a
  summary first, Passwords unticked (I36); Favorites and the Reading
  List as folders (I37); http and https visits, no redirect hops, the
  newest 100,000 (I38); passwords through PasswordImporter after the
  saved logins are read in full, replacing none (I39).
- Shared (I40, I42): one bookmark folder per source remembered by UUID
  (stedding.import.bookmark_folders), visits added only when the profile
  has none at that URL and time (checked on the history thread), import
  policies honoured, one import per source held by the profile rather
  than the page, one result line.
- Arc's importer gains ReadSafeStoragePassword, CopyChromiumFileForReading
  (journal, -wal, -shm) and a left-out count from ReadArcLogins.

Why: Dia users and people leaving Safari had no way to bring their
history and passwords, and Safari's own export is the one file it writes.
Removable when: never; the Settings and command bar rows (planned in
I32, I41) and Dia's sidebar (I33) build on this.
